Author: Fabian <fabian@schlieper.email>
Date:   Sat Sep 19 10:39:31 2026 +0200

    config: honour a top-level adapter: instead of ignoring it (#414)
    
    `adapter:` is documented as a per-BMS option, so a top-level one was read by
    nobody: the add-on silently kept using the default controller. That is
    indistinguishable from "the adapter I chose was selected and failed", which is
    the state the reporter of #414 was trying to debug on a two-controller Docker
    host.
    
